  "notes": "Drawn from 747-8Fs JA16KZ (2024), JA18KZ (2025) and JA14KZ (2026). In 2025–2026 several aircraft carry a small 40th anniversary badge on the aft fuselage (not drawn). The red pinstripe ends at a small red block by the wing; the belly isn't fully seen. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on JA14KZ (left, near level, 2026-03-20): 'Nippon Cargo' starts just behind the forward door at x 0.163 (not 0.13), runs 0.256, and its capitals reach y ~0.33 of the main deck's side, not 0.6 (cap 0.42; it had been ~40% too tall); lowercase 0.72 of the capitals. The 747's upper-deck hump is above it and isn't in the shapes.",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximate standard (a few colors from memory). NCA's blue 'NCA' scheme dates from its 747-8F era; earlier 747-200/400Fs wore an older blue-and-white scheme."
